			"author": {
				"name": "Lea Verou, PhD",
				"url": "https://front-end.social/@leaverou",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/298/949/173/613/152/original/4544b9a1d901ce42.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-17T21:00:21.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Yes!! I've been saying this FOR YEARS. If it takes effort to donate, most people just keep postponing it forever — or never think about it. And one day, it's too late. And relatives are usually too heartbroken to donate.</p>",
