			"url": "https://front-end.social/@lonekorean/109882741835552888",
			"author": {
				"name": "Will Boyd",
				"url": "https://front-end.social/@lonekorean",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/292/336/055/750/724/original/e577b97891570e9e.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-17T23:46:19.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> haha this struck a nerve in me I haven't thought about in years.</p><p>When I was a teen and got my driver's license, my mom told me not to be an organ donor because she felt weird about it.</p><p>Then my mom renewed hers a few weeks later and became an organ donor when she realized you got a discount for it.</p><p>She laughed it off but I was so pissed that me wanting to do the right thing was worth less than her $10 discount.</p><p>Sorry, venting, tangent, I agree with your point. 😄</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
